# gates/internal-names.allowlist
#
# INTENTIONAL public identifiers found by the full-tree internal-names gate.
#
# FORMAT: one 64-hex digest per line; sha256 of the name; comments start with
# '#'. A line whose first non-blank character is '#' is a pure comment and is
# ignored entirely, so comments may carry prose. Every other line must hold
# one or more 64-hex digests, separated by commas and/or whitespace. Any other
# token on a non-comment line is a hard load error - the gate prints the
# file:line and exits non-zero, rather than quietly widening the suppression
# set with a word from wrapped prose.
#
# A full-tree run of gates/check-internal-names.py reports 40 token-digest
# findings, all in pre-existing exchange documentation. Every one of them is
# one of the eight public council/exchange role identifiers listed below.
# These names appear in the public peer registry, the council proposal, and
# operating procedures. They are public by design, not private identifiers,
# so the PR gate (verify.yml, pull_request events) scans only changed files
# via `check-internal-names.py --diff-only` instead of failing every PR on
# these pre-existing lines. Push events still run the full-tree scan.
#
# This file names the identifiers in plain text on purpose, as the record of
# what is intentional. It is excluded from scanning via SELF_EXCLUDE in
# gates/check-internal-names.py and must stay excluded.
#
# Public role identifiers (8):
#   proteus, mozi, hazen, leo, frida, shaka, orda, lugia
